\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every minimal homeomorphism h of an infinite compact metrizable space X, is $rc(C(X)\rtimes _hZ)=mdim(X,h)/2$, allowing the value infinity? In particular is zero mean dimension equivalent to the small boundary property, Z-stability and finite nuclear dimension of the crossed product?

\subsection{Short English statement}
